 "summary": {
  "text": "Members are pushing back on a reported Trump administration plan, tied to Interior Secretary Burgum, to rename Lake Michigan \"Lake America.\" The volume is thin: eight posts from six members over four active days. @tedlieu opened August 25 with two posts and is the only member posting on more than one day; @RepMGS followed August 26; @RepDebDingell and @SeanCasten joined the August 27 peak of three posts, the only day with amplification; after a five-day gap @RepSaraJacobs and @sliccardo posted September 3. Framing moved from ridicule and misplaced priorities to shared heritage, then back to priorities with polling. Unclear whether any formal action exists, or whether Great Lakes members will coordinate.",
